Programme: #6894
Umbrella: #8212
Governance train: G2-delete
Depends on: #8723 with ruling = delete
Mutually exclusive with: G2-operate
Unblocks: #6894 governance closure and final crate cleanup

## Objective

Delete `perl_tdd_support::governance` when #8723 establishes that no accepted operational owner, input snapshot, baseline, gate posture, and receipt consumer justify retaining it. Remove the code, public contract, tests, dependencies, documentation, and capability claims rather than preserving dormant policy as a speculative library.

## End goal

The repository does not carry a configuration-rich ignored-test control that no real process uses. Every consumer is migrated or proven self-only/dead, public API and Cargo surfaces no longer advertise governance, and useful historical policy ideas remain in the issue/decision record rather than executable production-shaped code. Existing test-quality and ignored-test controls remain with their actual owners, without duplicate or shadow policy. This PR is deletion driven by an accepted ruling, not a redesign of ignored-test governance.

## Entry condition

Do not implement unless #8723's checked decision selects **delete** and records:

- no accepted operational/CI consumer;
- no accepted snapshot/baseline/receipt owner;
- no uncovered failure mode that existing controls fail to own;
- no evidenced external compatibility need requiring a temporary shim.

After the ruling lands, close the G2-operate and G3 issues as `not_planned`/superseded by this branch. If the ruling selects operate, close this issue instead.

## One-PR result

Delete, subject to current exact paths and #8418's consumer ledger:

- the `governance` module and public re-export;
- ignored-test inventory/policy/trend/report/alert/recommendation types;
- implementation and self-tests;
- governance-only dependencies/features/configuration;
- README/roadmap/API examples and claims;
- lint allowances or doctest exclusions retained only for this module;
- package/API ledger rows and generated projections that no longer exist.

Preserve the #8723 decision record and issue history as the rationale. Do not move dormant types into another crate before deleting them.

## Consumer handling

For every consumer found by #8723/#8418, choose one evidence-backed disposition:

```text
self-test/docs only → delete with module
real caller covered by another existing control → migrate to that owner
published compatibility with evidence → bounded deprecation shim or explicit release decision
unknown → resolve before deletion; do not assume dead
```

A compatibility shim may exist only if external evidence requires it, cannot execute or widen policy, and has an exact expiry/removal issue. The preferred result is no shim.

## Overlap and preserved controls

Document which existing mechanisms continue to own related concerns, including where applicable:

- panic/test-code ratchets;
- unwrap/expect policy;
- ignored/disabled test inventory or CI gates;
- no-assertion/silent-pass checks;
- generated status/quality receipts.

Do not modify those controls unless a direct compile/reference repair is required. Do not create a new ignored-test policy to replace the deleted one.

## Required proof

- #8723 decision digest/ruling is checked and selects delete;
- repository and Cargo consumer search shows no unresolved caller;
- crate default/all-features/docs/tests compile after removal;
- package contents and public API baseline exclude governance;
- #8418 public-surface ledger/projection has no stale governance row;
- dependency graph shows governance-only edges removed;
- docs/examples contain no current capability claim;
- negative package-boundary fixture reintroducing `pub mod governance` or equivalent unclassified policy fails;
- existing actual test-quality controls remain green and independently owned;
- no G2-operate/G3 implementation remains open as simultaneously selected work.

## Acceptance

- [ ] #8723 selected delete with the required evidence.
- [ ] Governance source, tests, docs, re-exports, dependencies, and capability claims are removed.
- [ ] No unresolved workspace or evidenced external consumer remains.
- [ ] No replacement dormant policy is moved elsewhere.
- [ ] Existing overlapping controls and owners are documented and preserved.
- [ ] #8418 ledger, API baseline, dependency graph, and docs are current.
- [ ] G2-operate and G3 are closed as not planned/superseded.

## Codex implementation guidance

Verify the ruling and current consumer graph before deleting anything. Remove the complete ownership family, then use compiler/API/package failures to expose hidden references, followed by explicit docs/Cargo/workflow searches that compilation cannot cover. Resist the temptation to save types or reports because they might become useful; preserve candidates in the decision record and delete executable code without an owner. Keep fixes to actual overlapping controls out of scope unless deletion directly breaks their reference.

## Non-goals

- No new ignored-test evaluator, snapshot, baseline, receipt, or CI gate.
- No generalized test-quality cleanup.
- No changes to TDD generation/cycle/runtime beyond removing governance references.
- No rewriting historical issue or commit evidence.

## Claim boundary

This PR proves dormant governance was removed after an evidence-backed no-owner ruling. It does not prove the repository needs no ignored-test control beyond the existing accepted mechanisms.

Parent: #8055
Train: #8686 A09
Depends on: #9448
Routing/enforcement: #3048 / #4787 / #4789
Release consumers: #6055 / #8576

## One-PR objective

Perform the first evidence-backed retirement/authority cleanup using #9448's inventory. Disable or delete only workflows proven orphaned, expired, obsolete, or duplicative; preserve useful specialized workflows with current owners.

For every changed workflow, record inventory classification, current callers/consumers, replacement or retirement reason, retained historical evidence location, context/policy references, and rollback/recovery where disabling rather than deletion is chosen.

Reconcile:

- orphan/expired temporary workflows;
- obsolete reusable workflows with no active caller;
- duplicate context producers;
- stale checked-in required-check references;
- authoritative workflow callers/consumers;
- historical evidence so executable YAML is not retained only for archaeology.

Deletion count is not a goal.

## Negative controls

- delete workflow still called by authoritative path;
- remove stable context without policy/consumer update;
- retire specialized workflow solely because it is uncommon;
- leave expired temporary workflow executable;
- delete workflow whose only historical evidence has not been preserved;
- source retirement contradicts live enablement/consumer state but is represented complete.

## Acceptance

- [ ] Every orphaned/expired workflow found in the first #9448 inventory has a reviewed terminal disposition.
- [ ] Active callers/policy/context references are reconciled before removal.
- [ ] Historical evidence survives outside obsolete executable YAML where needed.
- [ ] Canonical PR/main/nightly/candidate/publication/verification authority is easier to identify and unchanged except by reviewed transition.
- [ ] Live state uncertainty remains `not_proven`; no GitHub settings are silently mutated.

## Codex end goal

Land the first retirement/reconciliation PR only. Do not chase an arbitrary workflow count or remove useful specialized lanes to make the inventory smaller.
